ops.description:
Root ruling (2026-10-02): this is a required generic correctness fix. Keep it separate from the 276bcf2 runtime fix so the current verified image (tools fingerprint cdac6d28) can be tested unchanged. It lands before the next correctly rebuilt payload.

Defect: `internal/images/render.go:121,134-136` adds the `.claude/settings.json` copy tree only when `settings` is true, i.e. when the inventory has a branch marketplace. Consider an inventory that pins Claude plugins but has only ref marketplaces:
- its payload carries no `settings.json`, so it carries no `enabledPlugins`;
- the Go merge (`Scripts.EnablePayloadPlugins`) finds no image settings and does nothing;
- on a stock Sprite, whose `~/.claude/settings.json` already exists, every pin stays `enabled=false`;
- `check_plugins` then fails with an empty healthy list, the same failure fresh r3 hit.

The frozen 1da26d7d inventory is unaffected only because `claude-plugins-official` is on branch `main`.

Fix: add the tree when `settings || len(inv.Claude.Plugins) > 0`. The pack must then capture a `settings.json` that carries the build's user-scope `enabledPlugins`. This changes the rendered scripts and the tools fingerprint, so the image has to be rebuilt.
